        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 3,
          "name": "Removal of Director in Mumbai",
          "item": "https://www.patronaccounting.com/removal-of-director/mumbai"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can the Board remove a director?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Only shareholders can remove a director by Ordinary Resolution (>50%) at a general meeting under Section 169. Board cannot remove a fellow director. Special Resolution (75%) needed for independent directors in second term. Special notice under Section 115 is mandatory."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What resolution is needed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Ordinary Resolution (>50% votes cast) for regular directors. Special Resolution (75%) for independent directors reappointed for second term under Section 149(10). Special notice under Section 115 mandatory in both cases (at least 14 days before meeting). Patron manages voting and resolution."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does the director have the right to be heard?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes - fundamental right under Section 169. Director must be sent copy of special notice immediately, can submit written representation for circulation, can require it read at meeting if not circulated, and can speak at meeting even if not a member. Failing this invalidates removal."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a replacement be appointed at the same meeting?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, if special notice given for replacement too (Section 169(6)). Replacement holds office only for removed director's remaining term. If not filled at meeting: treated as casual vacancy (Board fills). Board cannot reappoint the removed director."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can the removed director claim compensation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Section 169(7) with Section 202: compensation = remaining term or 3 years (shorter) x average remuneration of preceding 3 years. For MDs with service contracts, additional severance per contract terms. Patron computes exposure before initiating removal."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What if the director challenges at NCLT?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Removed director (especially minority shareholder-director) can file under Sections 241-242 (oppression/mismanagement) at NCLT Mumbai Bench. If found oppressive, NCLT can restore director. Patron ensures procedurally perfect process to withstand challenge."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Section 169 apply to all directors?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Does NOT apply to: directors appointed by NCLT under Section 242 (only NCLT can remove), and directors appointed through proportional representation under Section 163. For all other directors including first, additional, nominee, and executive, Section 169 applies."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which ROC handles removal filings in Mumbai?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "ROC Mumbai at Everest House processes DIR-12 (cessation) and MGT-14 (special resolution) on MCA V3 portal. NCLT Mumbai Bench handles any challenges. Patron's Marine Lines office adjacent to ROC and centrally located for NCLT coordination."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}</script>

