<!-- SECTION 15A: LEGAL FRAMEWORK -->
<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal &amp; Compliance Framework for Director Removal</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Section 169(1):</strong> Removal by ordinary resolution after reasonable opportunity to be heard</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 169(1) Proviso:</strong> Independent director in second term &ndash; special resolution only</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 169(2):</strong> Special notice required for removal and replacement appointment</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 169(3):</strong> Company sends copy to director immediately; director entitled to be heard</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 169(4):</strong> Director can submit written representation for circulation</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 169(5)/(6):</strong> Replacement at same meeting; holds office for remaining term</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 115:</strong> Special notice &ndash; at least 14 days, not earlier than 3 months</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 167:</strong> Vacation of office &ndash; automatic for disqualification, 12-month absence</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 202:</strong> Compensation to removed director &ndash; remaining term or 3 years &times; avg remuneration</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 241-242:</strong> Oppression/mismanagement &ndash; NCLT challenge by removed director</li>
                    <li><strong>DIR-12:</strong> Cessation of director &ndash; filed within 30 days</li>
                    <li><strong>MGT-14:</strong> Special resolution filing &ndash; within 30 days</li>
                    <li><strong>ROC Mumbai:</strong> Everest House, 100 Marine Lines, Mumbai 400020</li>
                    <li><strong>NCLT Mumbai Bench:</strong> For oppression/mismanagement challenges</li>
                </ul>
                <p><strong>Filing Portal:</strong> <a href="https://www.mca.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mca.gov.in</a> (MCA V3) | <a href="https://nclt.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nclt.gov.in</a></p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ SECTION -->
<section id="faq-section" class="content-section" style="background-color: #ffffff;">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="faq-expanded">
                <aside class="faq-expanded__aside">
                    <h2 class="faq-expanded__title">Frequently Asked Questions &ndash; Removal of Director in Mumbai</h2>
                    <p class="faq-expanded__lead">Get answers about Section 169, special notice, resolution types, director rights, compensation, NCLT challenge, replacement, and applicability for Mumbai companies.</p>
                    @include('partials.bigin-form', [
                        'variant'  => 'compact',
                        'service'  => 'Removal of Director',
                        'city'     => 'Mumbai',
                    ])
                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can the Board remove a director?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. Only shareholders can remove by Ordinary Resolution (&gt;50%) at general meeting under Section 169. Board cannot remove a fellow director. Special Resolution (75%) for independent directors in second term. Special notice under Section 115 mandatory. Patron advises Mumbai companies on this critical distinction.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What resolution is needed?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Ordinary Resolution (&gt;50% votes cast) for regular directors. Special Resolution (75%) for independent directors in second term. Special notice under Section 115 mandatory (at least 14 days before meeting). Director must be given opportunity to be heard. Patron manages voting and resolution for Mumbai companies.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Does the director have the right to be heard?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes &ndash; fundamental right under Section 169. Director must be sent copy of special notice immediately, can submit written representation for circulation, can require it read at meeting, and can speak at meeting even if not a member. Failing this invalidates removal. Patron ensures strict compliance.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can a replacement be appointed at the same meeting?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes, if special notice given for replacement too (Section 169(6)). Replacement holds office for removed director's remaining term only. If not filled: casual vacancy (Board fills). Board cannot reappoint the removed director. Patron manages replacement appointment for Mumbai companies.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can the removed director claim compensation?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Section 169(7) with Section 202: remaining term or 3 years (shorter) &times; average remuneration of preceding 3 years. For MDs with service contracts, additional severance per contract terms. Patron computes compensation exposure before initiating removal for Mumbai companies.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What if the director challenges at NCLT?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Removed director (especially minority shareholder-director) can file under Sections 241-242 (oppression/mismanagement) at NCLT Mumbai Bench. If found oppressive, NCLT can restore director. Patron ensures procedurally perfect process &ndash; special notice, right to be heard, documented minutes &ndash; to withstand challenge.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Does Section 169 apply to all directors?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. Does NOT apply to: directors appointed by NCLT under Section 242 (only NCLT removes), and proportional representation directors under Section 163. For all others including first, additional, nominee, and executive directors, Section 169 applies. Patron verifies applicability before initiating.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which ROC handles removal filings in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>ROC Mumbai at Everest House processes DIR-12 (cessation) and MGT-14 (special resolution) on MCA V3 portal. NCLT Mumbai Bench handles any challenges by removed directors. Patron's Marine Lines office adjacent to ROC and centrally located for NCLT coordination.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Director ko kaise hataye?</strong> Shareholders hi hata sakte hain, Board nahi. Special notice do 14 din pehle. Director ko bolne ka mauka do. EGM mein Ordinary Resolution (&gt;50%) pass karo. DIR-12 file karo 30 din mein. Independent director (2nd term) ke liye Special Resolution (75%). Patron 35-50 din mein complete karta hai.</p>
                <p><strong>Kya director ko compensation milta hai?</strong> Haan, Section 202: bachi hui term ya 3 saal (jo kam ho) &times; pichle 3 saal ka average remuneration. MD ko service contract ke hisaab se additional severance bhi. Patron pehle compensation calculate karke batata hai.</p>
                <p><strong>Director cooperate nahi kar raha?</strong> Section 169 se hataao. Special notice, EGM, Resolution pass karo. Director resist kare toh NCLT mein challenge ho sakta hai &ndash; procedurally perfect process zaruri. Patron watertight removal handle karta hai.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

